Z||000018||FLASHY||09-26-2001||10:45 PM||||Wow, for a while there I thought it was unanimous that the bottom was better.<P>I agree in both cases...<P>TOP: Makes the car look slimmer, longer, and a bit more personality. But then again it also looks older-fashioned and slightly more domestic (less exotic in other words).<P>BOTTOM: More modern, can look lower to the ground, more agressive, more exotic, and less typical. But then again I think it makes the car look chubbier or bulky (not so streamline) and maybe a bit plainer.<P>I guess ultimately I'd have to have two fieros. One of each style.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks for the input so far everyone!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flash_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||10
