Z||000045||RRobinson||09-28-2001||11:17 AM||||Hey Steve,<BR>I like the top one...it looks cleaner, more honest, and accents the wheels. Monotone is nice, but gives it the "yep, it's been repainted" look. When I see monotone paint, I always wonder if it's an 88 GT.<BR>RR||||reg||1
Z||000046||FLASHY||09-28-2001||11:53 AM||||Hey Ryan, I know what you mean and I agree with you but the main reason I like monotone is because it has a more up-to-date look. From the perspective of someone who knows fieros, it seems normal or right to see them two-toned. But to the majority of people who see the car drive by it seems a bit dated. I guess I'm just getting too used to that look and want a change. I also prefer to be less common and more unique and therefore I feel making it monotone would put me one step further in that direction. I appreciate your (and everyone elses) opinion on this as it helps me get a sense of what people like. As it stands, I haven't painted it monotone yet and it's possible I may never do it but this is a good way to make decisions.<P>Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
